The basic idea underlying a co-operative society js that the members should themselves manage their own affairs and improve their economic lot in such mariner as they think appropriate subject, of course, to the relevant laws. An official person in charge is the last person to be contemplated for achieving the said purpose. We hope and trust that the Government shall not hereafter contend that once the term is over, the elected committee, even if it is not guilty of any irregularities and/or malpractices, has no right to continue in office and that they can appoint any one they like as person in charge. Indeed, this is the principle affirmed by a Full Bench of this Court in
M. Gidda Reddy v. Deputy Registrar, Kurnool (FB
).
